  "turns": [
    {
      "id": "t1",
      "instruction": "Build and analyze the two-tier triangular-prism space truss using OpenSees. The equilateral base has side length 4 m: A=(0,0), B=(4,0), C=(2,2*sqrt(3)) in the global XY plane. Levels 0, 1 and 2 have Z=0, 3 and 6 m. Use every node and member endpoint in the attached schedule: six inter-level chords, nine horizontal ties and twelve diagonals. Each side face of each tier has two crossing diagonals with no connection at their crossing. Fix the three base-node translations. All members are axial-only and all joints are pinned; rotational DOFs are inactive and may be numerically suppressed. In load case D, apply global Fx=+10 kN separately at A2, B2 and C2. Report ux, uy and uz at each top node, tension-positive axial forces in every chord and web member (include the horizontal ties), each base node's signed Fx/Fy/Fz reaction, and the signed sum of the three base reactions for each global direction. Use the complete attached node, member, property and load tables. Use first-order linear-elastic static analysis with self-weight, P-Delta, rigid diaphragms and rigid offsets disabled. State the load case, location, component, sign and unit for every result: m for displacements, kN for forces and kN.m for moments. Preserve the actual OpenSees version, runnable input, execution log and raw results, and check global equilibrium.\n\nUse the complete attached input tables. Global XYZ is right handed with Z upward; any planar model uses the XZ plane. All nodes listed are connected physical joints. Member local x points from i to j. In 2D local y=global +Y and local z=x cross y. In 3D local y=normalize(reference cross x), local z=x cross y; reference vectors are explicit. N is positive in tension. Signed section N/T/M2/M3 equal minus the i-end resisting action at the start and plus the j-end action at the end; V2/V3 use plus i-end and minus j-end action. Report global nodal displacements and support reactions; rotations follow the right-hand rule. Distributed loads act per actual member length, including inclined members. Use first-order linear elasticity with self-weight, rigid floors, rigid offsets, P-delta and construction stages off. Use only the specified cases and combinations. Compute every request in output-requests.json, retaining its location, side, signed component, unit and case/combination. Interior forces must include applied-load terms. Execute OpenSees and retain version, runnable input, current-model hash, run ID, actual solver log and raw result/case mapping. Report the requested results in the response body as well as structured results; independently check equilibrium. No numerical answer or native execution evidence is supplied.",
      "state": 1,
      "expectation": "analyze",
      "attachments": [
        "geometry.json",
        "properties.json",
        "loads.json",
        "output-requests.json"
      ],
      "unresolvedFields": [],
      "expectedQuestions": []
    }
  ],
